<title>NORWAY: Saga files to U.S. SEC to issue bonds.</title>
<headline>Saga files to U.S. SEC to issue bonds.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saga Petroleum ASA said on Friday it had filed with the United States Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) a shelf registration for issuance of public bonds up to $700 million.</p>
<p>The bonds are planned to be issued in the U.S. market between 1997 and 1999, Saga said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>It said the purpose of the registration was to establish a basis for further diversification for financing sources for the company.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
